    "plainEnglish": "This code describes a sudden, serious inflammation of the brain and spinal cord that develops rapidly, where the specific cause hasn't been identified. The condition occurs when the immune system mistakenly attacks nerve tissue throughout the brain and spinal cord, potentially causing symptoms like fever, headache, confusion, weakness, or difficulty with movement and coordination. It's a medical emergency that requires prompt treatment to prevent permanent neurological damage.",
