    "longDesc": "Tropical spastic paraplegia",
    "plainEnglish": "Tropical spastic paraplegia is a rare neurological condition that causes progressive weakness and stiffness in the legs, primarily found in tropical and subtropical regions. It is typically transmitted through blood transfusions or sexual contact with a virus called HTLV-1 (human T-lymphotropic virus type 1), though not everyone infected with the virus develops the disease. Patients experience increasing difficulty walking, muscle rigidity, and sometimes loss of bladder or bowel control.",
