    "longDesc": "Bacterial meningoencephalitis and meningomyelitis, not elsewhere classified",
    "plainEnglish": "This diagnosis means you have a bacterial infection that is causing inflammation in both your brain and the membranes surrounding it (meninges), and possibly your spinal cord as well. Bacterial meningoencephalitis is a serious condition that typically causes symptoms like fever, severe headache, stiff neck, confusion, and sensitivity to light. This code is used when doctors have confirmed a bacterial infection is the cause, but the specific bacteria hasn't been identified or doesn't fit into other more specific diagnostic categories.",
    "whoUses": "Neurologists, infectious disease specialists, and emergency medicine physicians use this code when treating patients with confirmed bacterial brain and spinal cord inflammation. This is a serious condition that commonly appears on hospital bills and EOBs, as it typically requires inpatient treatment with antibiotics and intensive monitoring, though it may not always be visible on initial urgent care or office visit statements.",
