    "plainEnglish": "Myelitis in diseases classified elsewhere refers to inflammation of the spinal cord (myelitis) that occurs as a complication of another disease you already have—rather than myelitis being the primary condition itself. For example, myelitis can develop as a secondary effect of infections, autoimmune diseases, or other systemic conditions. You would experience symptoms like weakness, numbness, pain, or loss of function in the areas of your body controlled by the affected part of the spinal cord.",
