    "plainEnglish": "An abscess is a pocket of pus caused by infection, and this code describes an infection that has formed in the layers surrounding your brain or spinal cord—specifically between the outermost membrane and the bone (extradural) or between two of the protective membrane layers (subdural). Symptoms may include severe headache, fever, neck stiffness, confusion, or neurological changes depending on the size and location of the infection. This is a serious condition requiring urgent medical attention and usually treatment with antibiotics or surgical drainage.",
