    "longDesc": "Sequelae of inflammatory diseases of central nervous system",
    "plainEnglish": "This code describes long-term complications or lasting effects that result from a previous infection or inflammation of the brain or spinal cord, such as meningitis or encephalitis. Even after the original infection has been treated and resolved, patients may experience ongoing problems like headaches, memory issues, weakness, balance problems, or other neurological symptoms that persist months or years later. These lasting effects are what doctors mean by 'sequelae'—the lingering consequences of the initial brain or spinal cord inflammation.",
    "whoUses": "Neurologists, infectious disease specialists, and primary care physicians use this code when evaluating patients with ongoing neurological symptoms stemming from past CNS infections. It appears on EOBs when patients seek treatment for persistent complications rather than the original acute infection, and is commonly used during follow-up care and rehabilitation visits.",
