    "shortDesc": "Congenital nonprogressive ataxia",
    "longDesc": "Congenital nonprogressive ataxia",
    "plainEnglish": "Congenital nonprogressive ataxia is a condition you're born with that affects your brain's ability to coordinate movement and balance, but it does not get worse over time. This means you may have trouble with walking, fine motor tasks like writing or picking up small objects, or maintaining your balance, but these symptoms remain stable throughout your life rather than worsening as you age. The coordination problems stem from how your brain developed before birth and are not caused by an injury or progressive disease.",
