    "longDesc": "Early-onset cerebellar ataxia, unspecified",
    "plainEnglish": "Early-onset cerebellar ataxia is a neurological condition where the cerebellum (the part of the brain controlling balance and coordination) is damaged or not functioning properly, causing symptoms to appear in childhood or early adulthood. People with this condition typically experience poor balance, uncoordinated movements, difficulty walking, tremors, and trouble with fine motor tasks like writing or picking up small objects. The specific cause isn't identified in this diagnosis code, but it usually results from genetic factors, developmental abnormalities, or inherited neurological disorders.",
