    "shortDesc": "Other motor neuron disease",
    "longDesc": "Other motor neuron disease",
    "plainEnglish": "This code describes a rare disorder affecting the nerve cells that control voluntary muscle movement, but it's not one of the more common types like ALS or spinal muscular atrophy. Patients with motor neuron diseases in this category typically experience progressive weakness, muscle wasting, or difficulty with movement, though the specific symptoms and rate of progression depend on which form of the disease is present.",
    "whoUses": "Neurologists use this code when diagnosing and treating patients with motor neuron disorders that don't fit neatly into standard categories like ALS or SMA. This code appears on EOB statements when patients are evaluated for unexplained muscle weakness or progressive neurological symptoms affecting motor function.",
