    "plainEnglish": "Spinal muscular atrophy is a rare genetic disease where nerve cells in the spinal cord gradually break down, leading to progressive muscle weakness and wasting throughout the body. When the type is unspecified, it means your doctor has diagnosed you with this condition but hasn't yet determined which of the specific forms you have (such as the infantile, juvenile, or adult-onset variety). You may experience increasing difficulty with movement, muscle loss, and eventually problems with activities like walking, lifting, or breathing as the condition progresses.",
