    "plainEnglish": "This code describes nerve and muscle damage that develops as a result of cancer elsewhere in the body, even though the cancer hasn't directly invaded the nerves or muscles. When someone has cancer, their immune system can sometimes mistakenly attack their own nerve and muscle tissues, causing weakness, numbness, or tingling. This happens as a \"side effect\" of the cancer rather than from the cancer itself spreading to those areas.",
