    "plainEnglish": "This condition occurs when severe, long-standing hypothyroidism (myxedema) causes damage and shrinkage of brain and nerve tissues. When thyroid hormone levels remain critically low for an extended period, the nervous system can deteriorate, leading to neurological symptoms like weakness, confusion, or movement difficulties. This is a rare complication that typically develops only when hypothyroidism goes untreated or severely undertreated for a long time.",
