    "shortDesc": "Malignant neuroleptic syndrome",
    "longDesc": "Malignant neuroleptic syndrome",
    "plainEnglish": "Malignant neuroleptic syndrome is a rare but life-threatening reaction that can occur when someone takes antipsychotic medications (also called neuroleptics). This condition causes a sudden onset of high fever, severe muscle rigidity, altered mental status, and dangerous changes in heart rate and blood pressure. Without immediate medical treatment in an intensive care setting, this syndrome can lead to organ failure and death, making it a medical emergency.",
    "whoUses": "Psychiatrists, neurologists, and emergency medicine physicians use this code when treating patients with severe adverse reactions to antipsychotic drugs. It commonly appears in hospital records and intensive care documentation rather than on routine outpatient EOB statements, as it represents an acute, serious complication requiring emergency hospitalization.",
