    "longDesc": "Secondary parkinsonism due to other external agents",
    "plainEnglish": "This diagnosis means you've developed symptoms similar to Parkinson's disease (like tremors, stiffness, or slow movement) as a side effect of exposure to certain external substances or toxins rather than from the disease itself. Common causes include medications (especially antipsychotics), exposure to pesticides or heavy metals, or other environmental toxins that affect the part of your brain controlling movement. The good news is that these symptoms may improve if the offending substance is removed or the causative exposure stops.",
