    "plainEnglish": "Hallervorden-Spatz disease is a rare, inherited neurological condition that causes progressive damage to nerve cells in the brain, particularly in areas that control movement. People with this disease typically develop symptoms in childhood or early adulthood, including muscle stiffness, tremors, difficulty walking, and progressive loss of mental function. The condition worsens over time and currently has no cure, though treatments can help manage symptoms.",
