    "plainEnglish": "Progressive supranuclear ophthalmoplegia (PSP), also known as Steele-Richardson-Olszewski syndrome, is a rare brain disorder that gradually damages nerve cells in areas that control eye movement, balance, and thinking. People with PSP experience increasing difficulty moving their eyes (especially looking downward), along with problems with balance, walking, speech, and memory that worsen over time. The condition typically appears in older adults and has no cure, though treatments can help manage symptoms.",
