    "shortDesc": "Degeneration of nervous system due to alcohol",
    "longDesc": "Degeneration of nervous system due to alcohol",
    "plainEnglish": "This code describes permanent damage to your nerves and brain caused by long-term heavy alcohol use. Alcohol is toxic to nerve cells, and chronic drinking can destroy the protective coating around nerves and kill brain cells, leading to problems like weakness, numbness, memory loss, balance issues, or difficulty walking. The damage is often irreversible, even if you stop drinking, though some symptoms may improve with abstinence and proper nutrition.",
