    "shortDesc": "Alpers disease",
    "longDesc": "Alpers disease",
    "plainEnglish": "Alpers disease is a rare, inherited neurological disorder that primarily affects infants and young children, causing progressive damage to the brain and liver. The condition leads to severe seizures, developmental regression (loss of previously learned skills), liver failure, and eventually fatal neurological decline, typically within the first few years of life. It is caused by mutations in genes that affect how the mitochondria (the energy-producing parts of cells) function.",
    "whoUses": "Neurologists, pediatric neurologists, and geneticists use this code when diagnosing and managing infants and young children with progressive seizures and developmental decline suspected to be caused by Alpers disease. This code rarely appears on routine EOBs but may be used for hospital admissions, genetic testing, or specialist consultations related to this serious pediatric condition.",
