    "shortDesc": "Mild cognitive impairment of uncertain or unknown etiology",
    "longDesc": "Mild cognitive impairment of uncertain or unknown etiology",
    "plainEnglish": "Mild cognitive impairment (MCI) means you're having noticeable difficulties with memory, thinking, or language that go beyond normal age-related changes, but these problems aren't severe enough to interfere significantly with your daily activities. The 'uncertain or unknown etiology' part means doctors have evaluated you and ruled out other specific causes (like Alzheimer's disease, strokes, or vitamin deficiencies), but they haven't pinpointed exactly what's triggering the cognitive changes. Many people with MCI remain stable over time, while others may progress to dementia, so your doctor will likely monitor you closely with regular cognitive testing.",
