    "rawCode": "G3185",
    "shortDesc": "Corticobasal degeneration",
    "longDesc": "Corticobasal degeneration",
    "plainEnglish": "Corticobasal degeneration is a rare, progressive brain disorder that causes gradual loss of nerve cells in specific areas of the brain that control movement, language, and thinking. People with this condition typically experience problems with coordination and balance, stiffness on one side of the body, difficulty with speech or understanding language, and progressive cognitive decline. Symptoms usually start in one limb and gradually spread, and the condition unfortunately worsens over time as more brain tissue deteriorates.",
    "whoUses": "Neurologists primarily diagnose and manage corticobasal degeneration, often with support from movement disorder specialists and neuropsychologists. This code commonly appears on EOB statements for patients undergoing diagnostic imaging (MRI), specialty consultations, and ongoing neurological care, though it is relatively uncommon compared to other neurological diagnoses.",
    "billable": true,
    "isNew": false,
