    "code": "G31.86",
    "rawCode": "G3186",
    "shortDesc": "Alexander disease",
    "longDesc": "Alexander disease",
    "plainEnglish": "Alexander disease is a rare, inherited neurological disorder that affects the white matter of the brain—the tissue that helps different brain regions communicate with each other. The disease is caused by mutations in a gene that produces a protein needed to maintain healthy brain cells, leading to progressive symptoms like developmental delays, seizures, weakness, and loss of coordination that typically begin in early childhood. Most children with this condition experience progressive worsening over time, though the severity and rate of progression can vary significantly between individuals.",
    "whoUses": "Neurologists and pediatric neurologists use this code when diagnosing and managing patients with Alexander disease, often after genetic testing and MRI imaging confirm white matter abnormalities. While this is a rare condition, it may appear on EOB statements when patients receive specialized neurological care, genetic counseling, or genetic testing related to their diagnosis.",
