    "shortDesc": "Other specified degenerative diseases of nervous system",
    "longDesc": "Other specified degenerative diseases of nervous system",
    "plainEnglish": "This code describes a degenerative disease of the nervous system that doesn't fit into other, more specific categories. Degenerative nervous system diseases involve the gradual breakdown of nerve cells and the structures they control, which can affect movement, sensation, memory, or other brain and nerve functions. If you see this code on your medical records, it means your doctor identified a condition affecting your brain or nervous system that is slowly getting worse, but it doesn't match the criteria for conditions like Parkinson's disease, Alzheimer's disease, or other named degenerative disorders.",
    "whoUses": "Neurologists, primary care physicians, and psychiatrists use this code when diagnosing patients with progressive nervous system conditions that are not otherwise specified. It's a catch-all code for unusual or atypical degenerative neurological presentations and may appear on patient EOBs when billing for office visits, imaging studies, or lab work related to nervous system evaluation and monitoring.",
