    "shortDesc": "Subac comb degeneration of spinal cord in dis classd elswhr",
    "longDesc": "Subacute combined degeneration of spinal cord in diseases classified elsewhere",
    "plainEnglish": "Subacute combined degeneration of the spinal cord is a serious condition where the nerve fibers in your spinal cord gradually break down, typically caused by severe vitamin B12 deficiency or other underlying diseases. This damage affects multiple areas of the spinal cord at once, leading to symptoms like weakness, numbness, tingling in your legs and hands, difficulty walking, and loss of coordination. It's called 'combined' because it damages different nerve pathways simultaneously, and it can worsen relatively quickly if the underlying cause isn't treated.",
    "whoUses": "Neurologists, hematologists, and internists use this code when a patient develops spinal cord damage secondary to conditions like pernicious anemia, B12 deficiency, or other systemic diseases. This code is less common on patient EOBs since it typically appears in hospital settings or specialist documentation rather than routine office visits, and it usually indicates a significant diagnosis requiring specialist evaluation.",
