    "longDesc": "Cerebellar ataxia in diseases classified elsewhere",
    "plainEnglish": "This code indicates that you have a loss of coordination and balance (ataxia) caused by damage to the cerebellum, which is the part of your brain that controls movement and balance. The cerebellar damage is occurring as a secondary effect of another disease or condition you have — it's not the primary diagnosis itself, but rather a complication or symptom caused by something else. You might experience unsteady gait, difficulty with fine movements, tremors, or difficulty with balance as a result of this cerebellar involvement.",
    "whoUses": "Neurologists most commonly use this code when documenting cerebellar dysfunction that results from an underlying disease (such as multiple sclerosis, paraneoplastic syndrome, vitamin B12 deficiency, or inherited neurological conditions). This code frequently appears on patient EOBs when neurological consultations are performed or when treating patients with complex conditions affecting the nervous system.",
