    "shortDesc": "Primary progressive multiple sclerosis, unspecified",
    "longDesc": "Primary progressive multiple sclerosis, unspecified",
    "plainEnglish": "Primary progressive multiple sclerosis (PPMS) is a type of MS where symptoms gradually worsen from the very beginning of the disease, rather than starting with relapses and remissions. In this form, patients experience a slow, steady decline in neurological function over time, with nerve damage in the brain and spinal cord causing progressive weakness, mobility problems, or other disabilities. Unlike other MS types where symptoms may improve between flare-ups, PPMS shows continuous progression without clear periods of improvement.",
    "whoUses": "Neurologists and MS specialists use this code to diagnose and document PPMS in patients with confirmed multiple sclerosis. This code commonly appears on EOB statements for patients receiving disease-modifying MS treatments, imaging studies (MRI), or specialized neurological care visits related to their progressive MS.",
