    "rawCode": "G35D",
    "shortDesc": "Multiple sclerosis, unspecified",
    "longDesc": "Multiple sclerosis, unspecified",
    "plainEnglish": "This code indicates that a patient has been diagnosed with multiple sclerosis (MS), but the specific type or pattern of the disease has not yet been determined or documented. Multiple sclerosis is a chronic autoimmune condition where the body's immune system attacks the protective coating of nerve fibers in the brain and spinal cord, causing communication problems between the brain and the rest of the body. Patients with MS may experience symptoms like fatigue, difficulty walking, numbness, weakness, vision problems, and cognitive changes, though symptoms vary widely from person to person.",
