    "plainEnglish": "Neuromyelitis optica (also called Devic disease) is a rare autoimmune condition where your immune system mistakenly attacks the optic nerves in your eyes and the spinal cord. This can cause sudden vision loss, eye pain, weakness, numbness, or paralysis in your legs or arms. It's related to multiple sclerosis but is a distinct condition that requires specific treatment to prevent further nerve damage.",
    "whoUses": "Neurologists and neuro-ophthalmologists primarily diagnose and manage neuromyelitis optica, often with input from rheumatologists for immunosuppressive therapy. This code appears on EOBs when patients receive MRI imaging, spinal taps, eye exams, or specialty consultations related to investigating or treating this condition.",
