    "plainEnglish": "You have a type of migraine headache that includes aura—visual symptoms like flashing lights, blind spots, or wavy lines that happen before or during the migraine. \"Intractable\" means your migraines are severe and don't respond well to standard treatment, making them difficult to control. This code indicates you're experiencing these hard-to-treat migraines but are not currently in an acute migraine attack.",
    "whoUses": "Neurologists and primary care doctors use this code when managing chronic migraine patients who fail to respond adequately to preventive and acute medications. It commonly appears on EOB statements for patients with documented resistant migraines, particularly those seeking specialist care or trying newer migraine therapies.",
