    "shortDesc": "Cluster headache syndrome, unspecified, not intractable",
    "longDesc": "Cluster headache syndrome, unspecified, not intractable",
    "plainEnglish": "Cluster headache syndrome is a rare but severely painful condition where you experience recurring cycles of intense headaches, typically on one side of your head around the eye or temple area. These headaches come in clusters (episodes lasting weeks or months) separated by pain-free periods, and each individual headache can last 15 minutes to 3 hours. The 'unspecified, not intractable' part means your doctor hasn't identified the exact pattern or severity details, but your headaches are currently manageable with treatment rather than resistant to all medications.",
