    "shortDesc": "Drug-induced headache, not elsewhere classified, intractable",
    "longDesc": "Drug-induced headache, not elsewhere classified, intractable",
    "plainEnglish": "This diagnosis means you're experiencing frequent, severe headaches that are directly caused by a medication you're taking, and the headaches don't respond well to standard treatment methods. The headaches are classified as 'intractable,' which means they're difficult to control or relieve, even with typical pain management approaches. Common medications that can trigger this type of headache include certain blood pressure drugs, hormonal therapies, and overuse of pain relievers themselves.",
