    "plainEnglish": "A thunderclap headache is a sudden, extremely severe headache that reaches its worst intensity within seconds to a few minutes—often described as feeling like you've been hit on the head. This type of headache happens without an obvious external trigger and is classified as \"primary\" when there's no underlying serious condition (like bleeding in the brain) causing it, though it still requires medical evaluation to rule out dangerous causes.",
