    "plainEnglish": "A primary exertional headache is a type of headache that occurs during or right after physical activity or exercise, such as running, weightlifting, or even sexual activity. Unlike migraines or tension headaches that happen for other reasons, this headache is directly triggered by the exertion itself and is not caused by an underlying brain condition or injury. The pain typically goes away within minutes to hours after you stop the activity.",
