    "whoUses": "Neurologists and primary care physicians use this code when diagnosing and treating patients with characteristic stabbing headache episodes. This code appears less frequently on patient EOBs than common headache types because primary stabbing headache is relatively uncommon, but it's used to document the condition for specialist referrals and when imaging studies have ruled out serious causes.",
