    "shortDesc": "Vertebro-basilar artery syndrome",
    "longDesc": "Vertebro-basilar artery syndrome",
    "plainEnglish": "Vertebro-basilar artery syndrome occurs when blood flow is reduced in the vertebral and basilar arteries, which are major blood vessels that supply the back of the brain. This can happen due to narrowing, blockages, or spasms in these arteries, and may cause temporary symptoms like dizziness, blurred vision, loss of balance, or weakness that come and go. Patients often experience these episodes without permanent brain damage, though the condition requires medical attention to prevent a stroke.",
