    "plainEnglish": "A brain stem stroke syndrome occurs when blood flow to the brain stem—the lower part of your brain that controls vital functions like breathing, heart rate, and swallowing—is blocked or interrupted by a blood clot or bleeding. This can happen suddenly and cause serious symptoms because the brain stem manages many critical life functions; patients may experience weakness, difficulty swallowing, dizziness, loss of coordination, or even paralysis depending on which part of the brain stem is affected.",
