    "longDesc": "Pure motor lacunar syndrome",
    "plainEnglish": "Pure motor lacunar syndrome is a specific type of stroke that occurs when a small blood vessel deep in the brain becomes blocked, damaging only the nerve fibers responsible for controlling movement. This condition typically causes weakness or paralysis on one side of the body (such as the face, arm, or leg) without affecting sensation, vision, or speech, distinguishing it from larger strokes that damage multiple brain functions. The word \"lacunar\" refers to the small cavity or hole left in the brain tissue after the stroke heals.",
