    "plainEnglish": "Pure sensory lacunar syndrome is a specific type of small stroke (lacunar stroke) that affects only the sensory nerves carrying touch, temperature, and pain signals from your body to your brain. This means you experience numbness, tingling, or abnormal sensations (like pins and needles) in an area of your body, but your muscle strength and ability to move remain normal. It typically occurs when a tiny blood vessel deep in the brain becomes blocked, and the symptoms usually appear suddenly on one side of the body.",
