    "plainEnglish": "Insomnia is a sleep disorder where you have persistent difficulty falling asleep, staying asleep, or getting quality sleep, even when you have enough time and opportunity to sleep. This unspecified code means your doctor has documented insomnia but hasn't identified a specific cause—it could be related to stress, anxiety, medical conditions, medications, or lifestyle factors. You may experience daytime fatigue, irritability, difficulty concentrating, or mood changes as a result of not getting enough restorative sleep.",
