    "plainEnglish": "This diagnosis means your internal body clock isn't synchronized with the normal 24-hour day-night cycle, so your sleep-wake schedule naturally \"drifts\" earlier or later each day. People with this condition often find themselves going to sleep and waking up progressively earlier or later than society expects, making it difficult to maintain a regular schedule for work, school, or daily activities. It's most common in people who are completely blind, since they can't receive light cues that normally help regulate the body's internal clock.",
    "whoUses": "Sleep medicine specialists, neurologists, and primary care doctors use this code when diagnosing circadian rhythm disorders. It appears on EOB statements when patients seek evaluation for chronic sleep scheduling problems, particularly those who are blind or have conditions affecting light perception.",
    "billable": true,
