    "shortDesc": "Primary central sleep apnea",
    "longDesc": "Primary central sleep apnea",
    "plainEnglish": "Primary central sleep apnea is a sleep disorder where your brain temporarily fails to send the proper signals to your breathing muscles during sleep, causing you to stop breathing for short periods throughout the night. This is different from the more common type of sleep apnea (obstructive), where your airway gets physically blocked—in this case, your airway is open, but your brain isn't telling your body to breathe. You might experience loud snoring, gasping awake, daytime fatigue, or morning headaches as a result.",
