    "whoUses": "Sleep medicine specialists, pulmonologists, and emergency/urgent care physicians use this code when evaluating patients with sleep disturbances at high altitude, particularly mountain climbers, people visiting ski resorts, or those relocating to mountainous regions. This code appears less frequently on routine patient EOB statements since it's typically diagnosed during sleep studies or specialist consultations for altitude-related symptoms.",
