    "shortDesc": "Congenital central alveolar hypoventilation syndrome",
    "longDesc": "Congenital central alveolar hypoventilation syndrome",
    "plainEnglish": "Congenital central alveolar hypoventilation syndrome (CCHS) is a rare condition that someone is born with, where the brain doesn't properly control breathing—especially during sleep or rest. Because the brain's respiratory control center doesn't send the right signals to breathe deeply enough, oxygen levels can drop and carbon dioxide can build up in the blood, which can be life-threatening if not managed with mechanical breathing support. Patients with this condition typically need ventilator support, especially at night, and require ongoing monitoring to stay safe.",
