    "plainEnglish": "This code describes various less common problems affecting the trigeminal nerve, which is responsible for sensation in your face and controls the muscles used for chewing. Unlike trigeminal neuralgia (which causes sharp facial pain), this category covers other nerve disorders that might cause facial numbness, weakness, tingling, or difficulty chewing. These conditions could result from nerve damage, inflammation, compression, or other medical issues affecting this important facial nerve.",
    "whoUses": "Neurologists, neurosurgeons, and primary care physicians use this code when evaluating facial nerve disorders that don't fit into more specific trigeminal nerve categories. It may appear on EOB statements for patients undergoing evaluation or treatment for unexplained facial symptoms, nerve testing, or imaging studies related to trigeminal nerve problems.",
