    "plainEnglish": "Melkersson's syndrome is a rare inflammatory condition that causes recurring facial swelling (typically affecting the lips and face), often accompanied by facial paralysis and a fissured tongue. The exact cause isn't fully understood, but it's believed to involve an abnormal immune or inflammatory response. Patients may experience episodes of facial puffiness that can come and go, along with difficulty moving one side of the face.",
