    "rawCode": "G520",
    "shortDesc": "Disorders of olfactory nerve",
    "longDesc": "Disorders of olfactory nerve",
    "plainEnglish": "This code describes problems with the olfactory nerve, which is the nerve responsible for your sense of smell. When this nerve is damaged or not working properly, you may experience a reduced ability to smell, a complete loss of smell, or distorted smells. This can happen due to infections, head injuries, neurological conditions, or other medical issues that affect the nerve itself.",
    "whoUses": "Neurologists, otolaryngologists (ENT specialists), and primary care doctors use this code when evaluating patients with smell disorders. It may appear on an EOB if a patient has seen a specialist for a smell complaint, though it's less commonly seen on routine patient statements compared to other diagnoses.",
