    "longDesc": "Disorders of multiple cranial nerves",
    "plainEnglish": "This code describes a condition where multiple nerves in your head and face (called cranial nerves) are not working properly at the same time. These nerves control important functions like eye movement, facial sensation, chewing, swallowing, and facial movement. When several of these nerves are affected together, you might experience symptoms like weakness in your face, difficulty moving your eyes, trouble swallowing, or loss of sensation in your face.",
    "whoUses": "Neurologists, neurosurgeons, and otolaryngologists (ENT specialists) use this code when patients present with dysfunction affecting two or more cranial nerves, often in cases of infections, tumors, stroke, or autoimmune conditions. It appears on EOB statements when patients undergo neurological evaluation and imaging for unexplained facial or head symptoms affecting multiple nerve functions.",
