    "rawCode": "G528",
    "shortDesc": "Disorders of other specified cranial nerves",
    "longDesc": "Disorders of other specified cranial nerves",
    "plainEnglish": "This code refers to problems affecting specific cranial nerves that don't fit into the more common categories. Cranial nerves are the twelve pairs of nerves that control functions like vision, hearing, facial movement, taste, and swallowing. When you have a disorder of these nerves—whether from injury, infection, inflammation, or other causes—it can result in symptoms like weakness, numbness, pain, or loss of function in the face or head area.",
    "whoUses": "Neurologists, otolaryngologists (ear, nose, and throat specialists), and primary care physicians use this code to document nerve-related disorders that don't have a more specific diagnosis. It appears less frequently on patient EOBs than codes for common conditions like Bell's palsy, but may show up when patients have complex or unusual cranial nerve problems being investigated or treated.",
