    "code": "G53",
    "rawCode": "G53",
    "shortDesc": "Cranial nerve disorders in diseases classified elsewhere",
    "longDesc": "Cranial nerve disorders in diseases classified elsewhere",
    "plainEnglish": "This code indicates a problem with one of the nerves in your head and face that is caused by another underlying disease or condition you have. Rather than being a primary nerve disorder on its own, this describes how a separate illness—such as an infection, autoimmune disease, or metabolic condition—is affecting your cranial nerves, which control functions like vision, hearing, facial movement, and sensation. You might experience symptoms like facial weakness, eye pain, hearing loss, or numbness depending on which cranial nerve is affected.",
    "whoUses": "This code is used by neurologists, primary care physicians, and specialists treating the underlying disease when a patient's main condition (such as diabetes, Lyme disease, sarcoidosis, or cancer) is causing nerve damage. It commonly appears on EOB statements when cranial nerve complications arise from a documented systemic disease and requires documentation of both the cranial nerve involvement and the causative condition.",
