    "shortDesc": "Brachial plexus disorders",
    "longDesc": "Brachial plexus disorders",
    "plainEnglish": "Brachial plexus disorder means there's a problem with the network of nerves that control your shoulder, arm, and hand. This bundle of nerves can be injured or compressed in different ways—from shoulder trauma, birth injuries, tumors, or inflammation—causing pain, weakness, numbness, or tingling in your arm. Depending on which part of the plexus is affected, you might have trouble moving your arm or lose sensation in certain areas.",
