    "plainEnglish": "Lumbosacral plexus disorders refer to problems affecting the network of nerves in your lower back and pelvis that control sensation and movement in your legs, feet, and pelvic organs. These nerves can be damaged or irritated by compression, injury, inflammation, or disease, leading to symptoms like pain, numbness, tingling, or weakness in the lower body. The specific cause might be a herniated disc, trauma, infection, or other conditions affecting this nerve network.",
