    "shortDesc": "Cervical root disorders, not elsewhere classified",
    "longDesc": "Cervical root disorders, not elsewhere classified",
    "plainEnglish": "This code describes problems with the nerve roots in your neck area that don't fit into more specific categories. Nerve roots are bundles of nerves that branch off from your spinal cord, and when they become irritated, compressed, or inflamed in the cervical (neck) region, you may experience pain, numbness, tingling, or weakness in your neck, shoulders, arms, or hands. This diagnosis is used when your doctor has identified a cervical nerve root issue but it doesn't match the criteria for more defined conditions like a herniated disc or specific nerve pinching.",
