    "plainEnglish": "Meralgia paresthetica is a nerve condition where the nerve running under your groin (the lateral femoral cutaneous nerve) becomes squeezed or irritated, causing numbness, tingling, or burning pain on the outer surface of both thighs. This happens most often when tight clothing, weight gain, or direct pressure irritates the nerve as it passes under a ligament in the groin area. When you have this condition on both sides of your body, it's called bilateral meralgia paresthetica.",
