    "shortDesc": "Idiopathic progressive neuropathy",
    "longDesc": "Idiopathic progressive neuropathy",
    "plainEnglish": "Idiopathic progressive neuropathy means you have damage to your peripheral nerves (the nerves that carry signals from your brain and spinal cord to your muscles and skin) that is getting worse over time, but doctors cannot identify a specific cause for it. You may experience symptoms like weakness, tingling, numbness, or pain in your hands and feet that gradually worsen as the condition progresses. Because the cause is unknown, treatment focuses on managing symptoms and slowing the progression of nerve damage.",
    "whoUses": "Neurologists and primary care physicians use this code when diagnosing patients with progressive nerve damage of unclear origin. This code commonly appears on patient EOB statements for those undergoing diagnostic testing, nerve conduction studies, or specialty neurology consultations to evaluate worsening nerve symptoms.",
