    "longDesc": "Radiation-induced polyneuropathy",
    "plainEnglish": "This diagnosis describes nerve damage that develops as a side effect of radiation therapy used to treat cancer or other conditions. When radiation beams are aimed at a tumor, they can also damage the nearby nerves that carry signals from your brain and spinal cord to the rest of your body. Patients with this condition typically experience weakness, numbness, tingling, or pain in their hands and feet that develops gradually over months or years after completing radiation treatment.",
    "whoUses": "Oncologists, radiation oncologists, and neurologists use this code when documenting a known complication of prior radiation therapy. It commonly appears on EOB statements for patients who have completed cancer treatment and are now experiencing nerve-related symptoms that are attributed to their radiation exposure.",
    "billable": true,
    "isNew": false,
    "isRevised": false,
