    "plainEnglish": "Polyneuropathy means you have damage to multiple nerves in your body, usually affecting your hands and feet, which can cause weakness, numbness, tingling, or pain. The 'unspecified' part means your doctor identified that you have this nerve damage but hasn't yet determined the exact cause—it could be from diabetes, infections, medications, vitamin deficiencies, or other conditions. You might experience symptoms like difficulty walking, loss of feeling in your extremities, or muscle weakness, and your doctor will likely order additional tests to figure out what's causing it.",
