    "plainEnglish": "Myasthenia gravis is a chronic autoimmune disease where your body's immune system mistakenly attacks the connection between your nerves and muscles, causing progressive weakness and fatigue in your voluntary muscles. This code indicates you have myasthenia gravis in a stable state without a current acute flare-up or worsening episode. You might experience muscle weakness that worsens with activity and improves with rest, particularly affecting your eye muscles, face, and limbs.",
