    "plainEnglish": "This code describes a condition where toxins or poisonous substances damage the connection between your nerves and muscles, affecting how your muscles receive signals to contract. Common causes include exposure to pesticides, certain medications, heavy metals, or botulinum toxin, and patients may experience muscle weakness, difficulty moving, or in severe cases, problems with breathing or swallowing. The damage occurs at the neuromuscular junction—the tiny gap where nerves meet muscles—which prevents normal muscle function.",
