    "plainEnglish": "Congenital and developmental myasthenia is a rare condition where the muscles don't receive signals from nerves properly, either from birth or developing in early childhood. This happens because of problems with how nerve signals are transmitted to muscles, leading to weakness and fatigue that typically worsens with activity and improves with rest. Patients may experience drooping eyelids, difficulty swallowing, weakness in facial muscles, or general muscle fatigue, and these symptoms usually appear in infants or young children.",
