    "rawCode": "G71036",
    "shortDesc": "Limb girdle musc dyst due to fukutin related protein dysfnct",
    "longDesc": "Limb girdle muscular dystrophy due to fukutin related protein dysfunction",
    "plainEnglish": "Limb girdle muscular dystrophy is a genetic muscle disease that primarily weakens the muscles around your hips and shoulders (your limb girdles), making it harder to walk, climb stairs, or lift your arms over time. This specific type is caused by a defect in a protein called fukutin-related protein, which your muscles need to function properly. Without this protein working correctly, your muscle fibers gradually break down and are replaced by fatty tissue, leading to progressive weakness.",
    "whoUses": "This code is primarily used by neurologists and genetic specialists who diagnose and manage muscular dystrophies, often after genetic testing confirms the specific protein defect. It appears on EOB statements when patients have genetic testing, neuromuscular imaging, or specialist consultations related to this inherited muscle disorder.",
