    "longDesc": "Other primary disorders of muscles",
    "plainEnglish": "This code refers to muscle disorders that don't fit into other specific categories—essentially a catch-all diagnosis for primary muscle diseases that affect how your muscles work or are structured. These are conditions where the problem originates directly in the muscle tissue itself (rather than from nerve damage or injury), and they can range from inherited genetic conditions to metabolic disorders that impact muscle strength, function, or appearance.",
    "whoUses": "Neurologists, physiatrists (rehabilitation medicine doctors), and muscle specialists use this code when diagnosing rare or unspecified primary muscle disorders. It appears on EOBs less commonly than specific muscle diagnoses, and is typically used after initial workup when a more precise diagnosis hasn't been confirmed yet.",
