    "shortDesc": "Primary disorder of muscle, unspecified",
    "longDesc": "Primary disorder of muscle, unspecified",
    "plainEnglish": "This code means you have been diagnosed with a primary muscle disorder, but the doctor hasn't specified exactly which type it is. Primary muscle disorders are conditions where the muscle tissue itself is weak or damaged, rather than the problem being in the nerves that control the muscles. You might experience muscle weakness, pain, or difficulty with activities like climbing stairs or lifting objects.",
    "whoUses": "Neurologists and primary care physicians use this code when a patient has muscle weakness or disease that hasn't yet been fully diagnosed or classified. It commonly appears on EOB statements as a placeholder diagnosis when more testing is pending or when the specific muscle disorder hasn't been definitively identified.",
