    "plainEnglish": "This diagnosis means you have muscle weakness or disease that was caused by exposure to a toxic substance—something poisonous or harmful that entered your body. This could be from medications (like certain steroids or statins used at high doses), industrial chemicals, alcohol used heavily, or other toxic agents that damaged your muscle cells. You might experience muscle pain, weakness, or difficulty with normal activities as a result.",
    "whoUses": "Neurologists, toxicologists, occupational medicine specialists, and primary care physicians use this code when evaluating patients with muscle damage linked to toxic exposures. It commonly appears on EOBs when patients have work-related chemical exposure, medication side effects, or substance-related muscle problems that require specialist evaluation or treatment.",
