    "longDesc": "Inclusion body myositis [IBM]",
    "plainEnglish": "Inclusion body myositis (IBM) is a rare, progressive muscle disease where your muscle fibers slowly break down and weaken over time. This condition causes the muscles in your legs, arms, and sometimes throat to gradually become weaker and smaller, making everyday activities like walking, climbing stairs, or gripping objects increasingly difficult. It's an inflammatory condition that develops slowly, typically in older adults, and unfortunately cannot be cured, though treatment can help manage symptoms and slow progression.",
    "whoUses": "Neurologists and rheumatologists typically diagnose and manage IBM, often confirmed through muscle biopsy showing characteristic inclusion bodies under a microscope. This code appears on EOBs for patients undergoing diagnostic testing, specialist consultations, or treatment monitoring for progressive muscle weakness.",
