    "plainEnglish": "Lambert-Eaton syndrome is a rare neuromuscular disorder where your immune system mistakenly attacks nerve endings, preventing muscles from receiving proper signals to contract. This condition occurs as a complication of cancer (most commonly small cell lung cancer), where cancer cells trigger the immune system to produce antibodies that damage the calcium channels in nerves. Patients typically experience muscle weakness that improves with exercise, fatigue, and difficulty with activities like climbing stairs or rising from a chair.",
