    "plainEnglish": "Spastic diplegic cerebral palsy is a movement disorder caused by brain damage that occurred before, during, or shortly after birth, primarily affecting both legs. People with this condition experience muscle stiffness and tightness (spasticity) mainly in the lower body, which makes walking difficult and often requires bracing, therapy, or mobility aids. The leg muscles tend to be overactive and rigid, while arm function is usually relatively preserved compared to other forms of cerebral palsy.",
