    "code": "G82.50",
    "rawCode": "G8250",
    "shortDesc": "Quadriplegia, unspecified",
    "longDesc": "Quadriplegia, unspecified",
    "plainEnglish": "Quadriplegia means all four limbs—both arms and both legs—are paralyzed or severely weakened, usually due to damage to the spinal cord or brain. This 'unspecified' code is used when the doctor has diagnosed quadriplegia but hasn't documented whether it's complete (total loss of function) or incomplete (some remaining function), or when the cause hasn't been fully specified. You would experience loss of movement and sensation in your arms and legs to varying degrees depending on the severity and location of the nerve damage.",
    "whoUses": "Neurologists, spinal cord specialists, physiatrists (rehabilitation doctors), and neurosurgeons use this code when documenting paralysis affecting all four limbs. It commonly appears on EOB statements for patients with spinal cord injuries, strokes, or other central nervous system conditions that affect movement in multiple limbs, and is often used as an initial or ongoing diagnostic code during treatment and rehabilitation.",
