    "rawCode": "G8251",
    "shortDesc": "Quadriplegia, C1-C4 complete",
    "longDesc": "Quadriplegia, C1-C4 complete",
    "plainEnglish": "Quadriplegia means all four limbs (both arms and both legs) are paralyzed due to a complete spinal cord injury at the highest levels of the neck (C1-C4 vertebrae). With a complete injury at these levels, there is total loss of movement and sensation below the injury site, and patients typically require significant assistance with breathing, eating, and daily activities. This is the most severe form of spinal cord paralysis and usually results from trauma like a car accident, fall, or diving injury.",
    "whoUses": "Neurologists, spinal cord injury specialists, physiatrists (rehabilitation doctors), and neurosurgeons use this code when documenting permanent paralysis from complete cervical spinal cord injury. It commonly appears on EOB statements for patients with catastrophic spinal injuries requiring ongoing rehabilitation, assistive devices, and long-term care management.",
