    "longDesc": "Quadriplegia, C1-C4 incomplete",
    "plainEnglish": "This code describes partial paralysis affecting all four limbs (arms and legs) due to an incomplete spinal cord injury in the neck region, specifically at vertebral levels C1 through C4. With an incomplete injury, some nerve signals can still pass through the damaged area, meaning the person retains some level of sensation or movement below the injury site—though the extent varies greatly from person to person. Patients with this condition typically have significant weakness or loss of function in their arms and legs, and may require mobility aids, specialized equipment, or personal care assistance.",
    "whoUses": "Physiatrists (rehabilitation specialists), neurologists, spinal cord injury specialists, and orthopedic surgeons use this code when documenting acute or chronic spinal cord injuries. It commonly appears on EOB statements for patients receiving rehabilitation services, physical therapy, occupational therapy, or ongoing management of spinal cord injury-related complications.",
