    "longDesc": "Quadriplegia, C5-C7 complete",
    "plainEnglish": "This code describes complete paralysis of all four limbs (arms and legs) caused by a spinal cord injury at the neck level between vertebrae C5 and C7. With this type of injury, the person has no voluntary movement or feeling below the mid-neck area, though they typically retain some arm and shoulder function since the nerve connections above that level are still working. This is one of the more severe forms of quadriplegia but less severe than injuries higher up in the neck.",
    "whoUses": "Neurologists, spinal cord injury specialists, physiatrists (rehabilitation doctors), and orthopedic spine surgeons use this code when documenting the long-term effects and management of cervical spinal cord injuries. It commonly appears on patient statements when someone is receiving ongoing treatment, therapy, or accommodations related to a documented neck-level spinal cord injury.",
