    "longDesc": "Quadriplegia, C5-C7 incomplete",
    "plainEnglish": "Incomplete quadriplegia from a C5-C7 spinal cord injury means you have partial paralysis affecting all four limbs (arms and legs), but you retain some muscle function or sensation below the injury level in your mid-to-lower neck spine. Unlike complete paralysis, incomplete quadriplegia varies widely—some people may have stronger arm function than leg function, or vice versa, depending on which nerve pathways remain partially intact. Your ability to move and feel will depend on the specific location and severity of the spinal cord damage.",
