    "longDesc": "Other specified paralytic syndromes",
    "plainEnglish": "This code describes a type of paralysis or weakness that doesn't fit into the more common paralysis categories. It could result from various causes such as nerve damage, spinal cord issues, stroke, or other neurological conditions affecting your ability to move certain muscles or parts of your body. If you see this code, it means your healthcare provider identified a specific paralytic condition but needed to use a broader category because it doesn't match the standard paralysis diagnoses.",
    "whoUses": "Neurologists, physiatrists (rehabilitation specialists), and primary care physicians use this code when documenting paralysis or motor weakness that doesn't fit standard diagnostic categories. It commonly appears on EOBs for patients undergoing neurological evaluation, physical therapy, or rehabilitation services, though it's considered a somewhat non-specific diagnosis that may be refined with additional testing or follow-up visits.",
    "billable": true,
    "isNew": false,
    "isRevised": false,
    "chapterId": 6,
