    "code": "G89.11",
    "rawCode": "G8911",
    "shortDesc": "Acute pain due to trauma",
    "longDesc": "Acute pain due to trauma",
    "plainEnglish": "This code describes sharp or severe pain that started recently as a direct result of an injury or accident. Whether you were in a car crash, fell, got hit, or had another traumatic event, this code captures the pain your body is experiencing in the immediate aftermath—typically the first few weeks to a few months after the injury occurred.",
    "whoUses": "Emergency medicine physicians, trauma surgeons, primary care doctors, and orthopedic specialists use this code when treating patients who have just suffered an injury. It commonly appears on EOB statements for emergency room visits, urgent care visits, and follow-up appointments for accident-related injuries.",
