    "plainEnglish": "This code describes ongoing pain that started from a past injury or traumatic event and has lasted for a long time—usually at least 3 months or longer. The pain persists even though the original injury may have healed or seems minor now, and it interferes with your daily life. This type of chronic pain can develop after accidents, falls, surgeries, or other injuries and often requires specialized treatment to manage.",
    "whoUses": "Primary care physicians, pain management specialists, physiatrists (physical medicine and rehabilitation doctors), and orthopedic surgeons commonly use this code. It frequently appears on patient EOB statements when billing for ongoing pain management visits, physical therapy, or other treatments aimed at controlling the long-term effects of past injuries.",
